I carefully pick up the second coffee.
I go towards the counter.
I feel very proud.
A woman is waiting there.
I place the cup on the counter in front of her.
I smile and say, "Here is your coffee, didi."
She looks at the coffee.
The coffee's foam has turned out perfectly.
She smiles and says, "Thank you!"
Hearing this, I feel very happy.
My first coffee had turned out bad.
But I have made this second coffee very well.
I am learning to operate the machine and make good coffee.
Sunita is also watching me.
She smiles looking at me.
Now I am ready to make the next coffee.
